---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title='About · Benji Tusk' description='About Benji Tusk and this engineering notebook.' width='prose'>
    <Hero title='About'>
        <Eyebrow slot='eyebrow' tone='accent'>Who's writing this</Eyebrow>
        <Fragment slot='lede'>
            I'm Benji — a computer science graduate who likes taking things apart to understand how they work.
        </Fragment>
    </Hero>

    <Prose>
        <p>
            <!-- Placeholder copy — edit freely. Written in the notebook's voice: honest, curious, understated. -->
            Most of what I build starts as a question I can't answer yet. How does this device actually talk to its driver?
            What is this protocol really doing on the wire? Could I make this run on Linux? I tend to follow those questions
            further than is strictly reasonable, and this notebook is where the results end up.
        </p>
        <p>
            I care more about the process than the polish. A wrong assumption I chased for three days is often more
            useful to write down than the tidy solution I landed on afterwards — so you'll find both here: the things
            that worked, and the ones that very much didn't.
        </p>

        <h2>What I work on</h2>
        <p>
            Reverse engineering hardware, writing Linux software, poking at I²C and USB, and learning whatever tool the
            current project demands. The subjects change constantly; the curiosity doesn't.
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
            The code lives on <a href={GITHUB_URL} target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>GitHub</a>, and you can
            reach me at <EmailLink />.
        </p>
    </Prose>
</BaseLayout>
